.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-BOOT-ASSERT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-boot-assert
.Nd check at every boot that the machine can boot again, and repair the boot path when it cannot
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
How a kldload machine boots is decided once, when it is installed, and
then changed by things that do not announce it: a firmware update or a
cleared CMOS wipes the boot entries, a distribution's boot-loader package
rewrites the fallback path, a network boot entry is put first.
The machine then fails at some later reboot, with nothing connecting the
failure to its cause.
.Nm
runs at every boot and re-establishes, in order:
.Bl -enum
.It
ZFSBootMenu,
.Pa \eEFI\ezbm\eBOOTX64.EFI ,
is on the EFI partition.
If not, nothing is guessed: it says so and exits 1.
.It
The fallback,
.Pa \eEFI\eBOOT\eBOOTX64.EFI
\(em the one path firmware boots with no boot entries at all \(em boots on
its own: it is ZFSBootMenu, or it is shim with the
.Pa grubx64.efi
shim loads beside it.
A missing fallback becomes ZFSBootMenu; a shim without its
.Pa grubx64.efi
gets one copied from the distribution's directory, or, with none to copy,
is replaced by ZFSBootMenu.
.It
There is a boot entry named
.Ql kldload ;
if not, one is made, pointing at the fallback when that is shim and at
ZFSBootMenu otherwise.
.It
That entry is ahead of every other on-disk loader in the boot order.
Network and removable entries in front are left in front: booting from the
network first is a choice this does not fight.
.El
.Pp
When nothing is wrong it writes one line.
Each repair is a line starting
.Ql REPAIRED ,
anything it cannot fix a line starting
.Ql FATAL
or
.Ql WARN .
Without a mounted EFI partition, or without UEFI, it has nothing to check
and exits 0.
.Pp
.Pa kldload-boot-assert.service
runs it at every boot.
It must run as root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the description at the top of the script and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
For testing:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_ESP
Check this directory instead of
.Pa /boot/efi .
The boot entries are still the real ones.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_BOOT_ASSERT_LOG
Log here instead of
.Pa /var/log/kldload/boot-assert.log .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/log/kldload/boot-assert.log
One line per run, one per repair.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Everything holds, repaired or already so.
.It 1
Something could not be repaired; the machine may not boot.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on 2026-09-30 by running it as root against a scratch EFI
partition in
.Pa /var/tmp/boot-assert-demo , with
.Xr efibootmgr 8
replaced by a script that prints a fixed boot list, so that no boot entry
could be changed.
Each case starts from a fresh partition holding only ZFSBootMenu, set up
as its heading says; after the exit status is the log.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
== fallback missing
exit 0
[2026-09-30 02:02:07] REPAIRED: /var/tmp/boot-assert-demo/esp/EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI was missing — installed ZFSBootMenu there
== all good
exit 0
[2026-09-30 02:02:07] boot invariants OK
== fallback is shim without grubx64.efi
exit 0
[2026-09-30 02:02:07] REPAIRED: fallback was shim with no grubx64.efi — restored from /boot/efi/EFI/fedora/grubx64.efi
== ZFSBootMenu missing
exit 1
[2026-09-30 02:02:07] FATAL: /var/tmp/boot-assert-demo/esp/EFI/zbm/BOOTX64.EFI is missing — cannot assert or repair the boot path
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr efibootmgr 8 ,
.Xr kldload-journal-assert 8 ,
.Xr kldload-secure-boot 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-08-25 an install shipped shim at the fallback path with the
.Pa grubx64.efi
it loads deleted; it went unnoticed because the boot entry still worked,
until a machine whose firmware preferred its own entry.
The boot-order step was described in this tool from the start and written
after 2026-09-07, when a network entry pushed ZFSBootMenu to last and a
server booted through grub instead, without its boot environments.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
With Secure Boot on, replacing a shim that has no
.Pa grubx64.efi
with ZFSBootMenu gives a fallback the firmware will not start; it could
not start the shim either.
.Pp
The distribution directories it copies
.Pa grubx64.efi
from are always read under
.Pa /boot/efi ,
whatever
.Ev KLDLOAD_ESP
says.
